In case you still don't get how huge Silencio could be, then you might have missed this:

Like a month ago, the Gates Foundation pulled together a 60-member coalition, Anthropic, Google, OpenAI, Microsoft, NVIDIA, ElevenLabs and many more, with one shared 5-year goal:

give 3.4 billion people access to AI in their own language and voice. that means closing the gap across more than 7,000 languages, most of which barely have the voice data to train on.

in other words, the biggest institutions and leading AI labs on earth have confirmed that voice data for underrepresented languages is one of the most important problems in AI right now.

that's the exact market @silencioNetwork has been building for this whole time, and likely no other firm in the world can serve niche languages from 2.5M+ people across the globe the way they can.

given the timing and relevance, maybe the most exciting DePIN in the entire space right now. and the fact that they're already working with some of the leading AI labs as paying clients validates exactly that.

